* Named characters, and the idioms that print them.
*
* An included file declares: names, and macros made of them. It cannot emit
* BrainFuck, which is why there is not a single instruction below that is not
* inside a `@macro` -- and why the instructions this file describes report the
* line that invoked them rather than a line of a file nobody opened.

@define NL 10
@define SPACE 32

* Empty the cell under the cursor. The idiomatic clear: `[+]` also works and
* takes about 256 iterations to do it.
@macro clear {
    [-]
}

* Put a value in the cell under the cursor, whatever it held before.
@macro set(value) {
    @clear
    +{value}
}

* Print one character, and leave the cell holding it.
@macro put(letter) {
    @set(letter)
    .
}
